{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":3,"query":"name=Feynman&limit=10&title=QED","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"QED","subTitle":"a play"},"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Parnell, Peter.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips."},{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Feynman, Richard P. (Richard Phillips)",{"@type":"date","#text":"1918-1988"}]}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"gsafd","#text":"Historical drama"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Drama"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Milwaukee, WI"}}],"publisher":["Applause Theatre & Cinema Books","Sales & distribution [in] North America [by] Hal Leonard Corp."],"dateIssued":["c2002",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2002"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"vii, 54 p. ; 23 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"The late physicist Richard Feynman is the subject of Peter Parnell's nearly one-man show, QED, a recent Broadway triumph for Alan Alda in the role of Feynman. Set in Feynman's office on the weekend in which he discovers he has terminal cancer, this play is a tour-de-force that captures his unique and puckish genius. As we read about his work on the Manhattan Project, his reconstruction of the space shuttle Challenger disaster, and his Nobel prize-winning quantum electrodynamics theory, as well as the intimate details of Feynman's personal life, we grow to love the man behind the science. And we read in fascination as he puzzles over the problem of his own death to a powerful conclusion. With a thoughtful foreword from Alda, this is a moving play that is a must for science and theatre fans everywhere.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"note":{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by Peter Parnell ; inspired by the writings of Richard Feynman, and Ralph Leighton's Tuva or bust! ; with a foreword by Alan Alda."},"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips"},"genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Feynman, Richard P. (Richard Phillips)",{"@type":"date","#text":"1918-1988"}]},"genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Quantum electrodynamics","genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Cancer","Patients"],"genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Terminally ill","genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Atomic bomb","genre":"Drama"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Physicists","genre":"Drama"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"PS3566.A752 Q43 2002"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"812/.54"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Tuva or bust!"},"name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Leighton, Ralph."}},{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"QED"},"name":{"namePart":"Parnell, Peter."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York, NY : Applause Theater & Cinema Books ; Milwaukee, WI : Distribution by Hal Leonard Corp., ©2002"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)606897832"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990089867620203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1557835926"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2002008311"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"50004999"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Scien